ant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA NOBUHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YABUNOUCHI NOBUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKOTA KIYOHIKO</name><address><country>US</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA, NOBUHIDE</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YABUNOUCHI, NOBUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOTA, KIYOHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA NOBUHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YABUNOUCHI NOBUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKOTA KIYOHIKO</name><address><country>US</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA, NOBUHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YABUNOUCHI, NOBUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOTA, KIYOHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A catalyst for olefin/styrene copolymerization which comprises (A) a transition metal compound, (B) a compound capable of forming an ionic complex together with an oxygenic compound or a transition metal compound, and (C) a specific compound, e.g., a product of the reaction of triphenylmethyl alcohol with triisobutylaluminum, and optionally contains (D) an alkylating agent; and a process for producing an olefin/styrene copolymer with the catalyst. The catalyst has improved activity in polymerization, so that the amount of a promoter to be used, such as an oxygenic compound, can be reduced. Thus, an olefin/styrene copolymer can be efficiently produced at a low cost.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention se rapporte à un catalyseur pour la copolymérisation d'oléfine/styrène, qui comprend: (A) un composé de métal de transition; (B) un composé capable de former un complexe ionique avec un composé d'oxygène ou un composé de métal de transition; et (C) un composé spécifique, constitué par exemple par le produit de la réaction d'alcool triphénylméthylique avec du tri-isobutylaluminium; et éventuellement (D) un agent d'alkylation; ainsi qu'à un procédé de production d'un copolymère d'oléfine/styrène à l'aide de ce catalyseur. Ce catalyseur possède une plus grande activité polymérisante, ce qui permet de réduire la quantité de l'agent promoteur devant être utilisé, par exemple un composé d'oxygène. Ainsi, un copolymère d'oléfine/styrène peut être produit efficacement à faible coût.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>